'=====================================================================
' Agent name : BulkReg\08 - Repair Missing Mail Files
' Version    : 4.4.0  (BulkReg release; libraries BulkRegCommon + BulkRegAgents 4.4.0)
' Code       : ALL logic is in the script library BulkRegAgents (BR_RunRepairMail).
'              This agent only calls it, so it never changes between releases.
'
' HOW TO INSTALL: open the agent, click in the editor, Ctrl+A, Delete, paste this
'              WHOLE file, Ctrl+S. Designer puts each part in its place automatically.
' Designer   : Shared agent, LotusScript
'              Runtime: On event > Action menu selection, Target: None
'              (NOT 'All selected documents' - Designer's default - or Notes asks for a selected document)
'              (backslash in the name = Actions > BulkReg submenu; do NOT use '|')
'
' What it does (details: BulkRegAgents > BR_RunRepairMail):
'
' Creates the mail files that are missing for REGISTERED users (and reports incomplete ones). It
' replaces the retired agent 07 - Create Mail Files. It works from the Domino Directory, not from batch
' files, so it also repairs users whose batch file / results file is gone and users registered by an
' interrupted run. Scope: all users, one mail server, or one batch file.
' Fast: one database list per server, the mail template opened once, work in chunks of
' MailRepairChunkSize (default 10) with an adaptive pause, STOP.txt for a clean stop.
' Never overwrites an existing mail file; a file with documents is never touched.
' DryRun=1 (default) only reports (WOULD_CREATE). LIVE: type REPAIR to confirm.
' Report: <BatchDir>\<scope>_mailrepair_<MODE>_<run>.csv + audit folder + log database.
'=====================================================================
'#####################################################################
' --- part 1: (Options) ---
'#####################################################################
Option Public
Option Declare
Use "BulkRegAgents"
'#####################################################################
' --- part 2: Initialize ---
'#####################################################################
Sub Initialize
	Call BR_RunRepairMail()
End Sub
